cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the associated paper as follows."
title: "DORA: Object Affordance-Guided Reinforcement Learning for Dexterous Robotic Manipulation"
abstract: >-
  An object affordance-guided reinforcement learning framework that enables a multi-fingered
  robotic hand to learn human-like manipulation strategies more efficiently. Affordance maps
  generate semantically meaningful grasp-pose candidates used as policy constraints and priors,
  combined with a voting-based grasp classification mechanism and an affordance-aware reward.
  Improves task success rates by an average of 15.4% over baselines across cube grasping, jug
  grasping/lifting, and hammer use.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - reinforcement learning
  - dexterous manipulation
  - object affordances
  - grasping
